    (162, "chat_create needs for: me for a chat you lead (it asks you, not a person, and its claims are yours to check before you pass them on: skill stillfail-leading), person for one opened for your person (theirs: you are told nothing of it). A chat headed 由…领导的/Led by <a chat's link> asks its leader (need_human reaches it, not a person) and gives what it would drop as a proposal; one headed …为你开的/Opened for you by is your person's."),
    (163, "station_move plan and status answer a summary (each module's counts, what cannot move grouped by why with a few examples, what moving an item alone would stop, what is lent and what is stopped); a module's items come a page at a time with module (after, limit), one with item; its `room` says the chats' files in bytes and what is free there, and a move that would not leave that station 20 GB (or a tenth of its disk) free is refused (skill stillfail-move)."),
    (164, "browser takes engine (chrome or farview: this chat's browser, kept for it, where the station has Farview) and, on Farview, action open (url) and close (tab), tab for endpoint and status: a chat's Farview tabs share one profile, and a page's new window is a tab of its own."),
    (165, "Pi is available where the station has Pi 1.0 or newer installed and a profile it runs on (a provider's key, an OpenCode Go or Anthropic key, or custom variables): chat_create takes runtime \"pi\"."),
    (166, "Messages can come from group (IM) chats, via=\"group\": a conversation's thread is its id twice (a private chat calls you with every message, a group with an @ of your name); mention people as @name; a card shows there as its question and numbered options in the text, and the answer comes as the option's words; chat_leave stops following a group until someone mentions you again."),
    (167, "Antigravity CLI (agy) sessions now load the workspace's and preset's skills, tell a repository's AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md files when tools touch it, and default multi-level models to medium unless another level is chosen; after an account or runtime switch on a spent limit, post a brief progress note if what remains will take more than a couple of minutes and people have not yet been told the plan."),
    (168, "chat_create takes speed: standard, fast or ultrafast. Ultrafast needs GPT-6 Astra or GPT-6.1 Sol on a Codex subscription with an eligible OpenAI plan; the legacy fast switch still works."),
    (169, "A login, vault, phone, rig or sign-in card now waits until it is decided or you withdraw it (secret_cancel and the like), whatever people write meanwhile, so secret_reask and phone_use reask are needed only for one you withdrew; an options or text card in a Slack, Feishu or group thread ends only as a message reaches you there. A post with a card still pending that ends your turn with no state ends it need_human; after a post, a turn with no state ends all_done after one reminder."),
    (170, "Moving to another station is a test-channel feature of the station's: on a station updated on the stable channel there is no station_move tool and your instructions do not name skill stillfail-move."),
    (171, "Skill stillfail-browser now covers Farview (driven with its agent.exe, not DevTools) as well as Chrome, and `browser {engine}` to switch."),
    (172, "station_task `dir` now brings a repository's Git submodules too: the target checks each out in the mirror at the commit the source has before the command runs (its commit must be pushed, or in the target's own clones); see skill stillfail-jobs."),
    (173, "feedback_send takes desktopPlatform when the affected desktop app is known, so its fix is announced on that platform’s release."),
