    (176, "relays action enroll (name) now issues a one-use workspace mesh relay enrollment token, valid for 24 hours. Keep it private; it grants forwarding only and is redeemed at the issuing station. list includes registered mesh nodes; revoke (node) asks the issuing station to remove one."),
    (177, "station_version: list shows this station's release, its channel's latest and the earlier releases it can go back to; update installs the latest; back {to} goes back to one of them when the latest broke something (updating by itself pauses until a newer release is out)."),
    (178, "New tool chat_configure: inspect or change a session's runtime, model, effort, speed, context, preset or account (repick) here or on another workspace station; omit chat or pass \"self\" for your own. chat_list now shows each session's model and creator and accepts model, created_by (\"me\" or email), archived and station (name/id or \"all\") filters. Superseded tools (adb_devices, phone_use, secret_reask, station_retire) are hidden from tools/list in favor of device_list/device_use and station_move."),
    (179, "Moving to another station is on for every station now, stable ones too: station_move and skill stillfail-move are there wherever a station did not offer them before."),
    (180, "chat_post now takes a Feishu chat_id as to (to=\"oc_…\"): in a Feishu group your bot made or is in, with no conversation yet, it posts the first message there and makes that thread one of your conversations; its answer names the oc_…/… address to use from then on."),
    (181, "Google Colab GPU sandboxes (colab-g4, colab-l4, colab-t4) are now automatically exposed from Google Colab profiles in Settings → Profiles (设置 → Profiles) and discoverable across stations in the same workspace via station_list and station_task."),
    (182, "chat_configure now takes for: \"me\" (lead a still.fail chat as your sub-chat) or \"person\" (hand a led sub-chat back to people), and reports led and leader when inspecting a session."),
    (183, "station_version now supports action: \"wait\" (until: [\"pr:N\", \"fix:FB-N\", \"commit:SHA\", \"version:0.1.N\", \"after:0.1.N\"], or clear: true) to auto-update once a release contains specified fixes; list also reports overridden, overrideBase, overrideKind, overrideNote, autoWhen and autoHeld when applicable."),
    (184, "Post brief progress updates with chat_post during long multi-step waits instead of looping silently; when a turn stays open after declaring waiting (such as a background command in agy), the station now wakes it once its waiting timer runs out."),
    (185, "chat_post now takes kind waiting with for and seconds: a post saying what you started can end the turn itself. A need that says nothing is needed (无需操作) is refused: use waiting for your own running work."),
    (186, "chat_configure now takes project (\"\" for cross-project) and tags/tags_add/tags_remove (max 3) to silently classify chats; new tool project_manage (read skill stillfail-projects first) lists, proposes new projects (never end need_human for a proposal), updates shared project info, renames, merges, or bulk reclassifies."),
    (187, "In Antigravity CLI, search is now declared directly alongside skill_read; when a workspace has more skills than fit .agent/skills, the omitted ones stay searchable with search (kinds=[\"skill\"]) and readable with skill_read."),
    (188, "Projects are conceptual workstreams (e.g. office CI, ops, clients, products, research — not limited to GitHub repos or folders); unclassified and empty project are unified (no separate cross-project bucket). Tags (0–3) are optional: prefer existing tags and leave tags empty when unsure instead of inventing ad-hoc tags. Accepting project_manage(action=\"propose\") only creates the project without auto-assigning the current chat. project_manage(action=\"reclassify\") now batches per station up to 500 items and accepts optional station (name or id) on each item; chat_list also accepts project (\"\" for unclassified)."),
    (189, "chat_list now supports offset (pagination) and compact: true (one-line `- <address> \"<title>\" [...]` summary with limit up to 500) for scanning large chat lists."),
    (190, "Memory now routes into four layers: MEMORY.md (<= 8 KB target, hard-capped at 16 KB on injection) for cross-project/person/machine rules only, skills/<project>/SKILL.md for projects, skills/machines/<station-tag>.md for machine/environment notes (current station auto-injected as <station-memory>, 4 KB cap), and skills/people/<name>.md for team roles and preferences (read via skill_read). Update existing same-topic entries in place instead of appending duplicates."),
    (191, "skills/people/<person-tag>.md (the tag is the person's email in lower case) of the person a session is for is now auto-injected at session start as <person-memory> (4 KB cap): keep personal preferences, approval habits and personal machine details there, not in MEMORY.md."),
    (192, "device_list now includes AirPlay devices (kind: \"airplay\", Apple TV / HomePod / AirPlay speakers) and new tool device_control runs standard AirPlay actions (status, power, remote, apps, launch, playing, seek, volume, keyboard, play_url, stream_audio) over the device tunnel (see skill stillfail-jobs)."),
    (193, "station_tool called with no name lists every tool it reaches (with what each does): call it so first when its description names no tools."),
    (194, "chat_post takes reply_to in a Feishu conversation: the ts of a message there to post under, in its thread, so a group is not interrupted; left out, the post goes where the conversation is. Choose where each post belongs."),
    (195, "When choosing a specific model with chat_create, pass both its full model ID and its runtime, because passing only model uses the opening chat's runtime."),
    (196, "For read-only inspection of a shared repository cache clone (history, search, diff on a fixed commit), run `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 git -C <repos_dir>/<repo> grep|show|diff|log` without opening a worktree (or open a CoW worktree if a partial clone lacks blobs); when editing or building, use `stillfail -C <repos_dir>/<repo> worktree add --detach <workspace>/<name> origin/main` for a copy-on-write worktree."),
    (197, "Platform attachments (Slack, Feishu, group, Comma) are no longer eagerly downloaded by the station; they appear under Unfetched files with their file ids. Call chat_history with to and fetch=[\"<id>\"] to download what you need (the station deduplicates and coalesces downloads across calls and sessions)."),
  ]
}

fn note_visible(n : Int, projects_on : Bool) -> Bool {
  if is_projects_gated(n) {
    projects_on
  } else {
    true
  }
}

/// Next `told_notes` value after delivering all currently visible notes to a session at `told`.
/// Low 20 bits hold the highest note number reached; upper bits record gated features skipped.
pub fn next_told(told : Int, projects_on : Bool) -> Int {
  let prev_mark = told & WATERMARK_MASK
  let mut withheld = told & (0 - 1 - WATERMARK_MASK)
  let mut max_mark = prev_mark
  let notes = migration_notes()
  for i in 0..<notes.length() {
    let (n, _) = notes[i]
    if n < REWRITTEN {
      continue
    }
    let gated = is_projects_gated(n)
    if note_visible(n, projects_on) {
      if n > max_mark {
        max_mark = n
      }
      if gated {
        withheld = withheld & (0 - 1 - GATED_PROJECTS_BIT)
      }
    } else if gated && n > prev_mark {
      withheld = withheld | GATED_PROJECTS_BIT
    }
  }
  max_mark | withheld
}

pub fn latest_told(projects_on : Bool) -> Int {
  next_told(0, projects_on)
}

pub fn untold_entries(told : Int, projects_on : Bool) -> Array[(Int, String)] {
  let prev_mark = told & WATERMARK_MASK
  let withheld = told & (0 - 1 - WATERMARK_MASK)
  let notes = migration_notes()
  let out : Array[(Int, String)] = []
  for i in 0..<notes.length() {
    let (n, text) = notes[i]
    if n < REWRITTEN || !note_visible(n, projects_on) {
      continue
    }
    if n > prev_mark {
      out.push((n, text))
    } else if is_projects_gated(n) && (withheld & GATED_PROJECTS_BIT) != 0 {
      out.push((n, text))
    }
  }
  out
}

pub fn has_untold(told : Int, projects_on : Bool) -> Bool {
  untold_entries(told, projects_on).length() > 0
}

pub fn untold_notes(told : Int, full_path : String, projects_on : Bool) -> String {
  let entries = untold_entries(told, projects_on)
  if entries.length() == 0 {
    return ""
  }
  let lines : Array[String] = []
  for i in 0..<entries.length() {
    let (_, note) = entries[i]
    lines.push("- " + note)
  }
  "[still.fail changed how you work since this session began]\n" +
  join_strings(lines, "\n") +
  "\nToday's whole instructions, tool parameters included, are in " +
  full_path +
  ": read them when you need the details (your tool list may not show the new parameters; pass them anyway)."
}
